# PCF stack lock

Virtual control. Host provides React and Fluent via platform libraries. **Do not change these versions.**

| Library | Version | Where |
|---|---|---|
| React / react-dom | **16.14.0** | `package.json` + `<platform-library name="React">` |
| @fluentui/react-components | **9.46.2** | `package.json` + `<platform-library name="Fluent">` |
| @fluentui/react-icons | **2.0.335** | `package.json` only (allowed) |

## React 16 limits

Hooks and `React.FC` are fine. Do **not** use React 18 APIs (`createRoot`, `useId`, `useTransition`, `useDeferredValue`, `useSyncExternalStore`) or React 19 features.

## Allowed packages

Only browser-safe, PCF-supported libraries. Default allowlist:

- `@fluentui/react-components@9.46.2` (do not add other Fluent major versions)
- `@fluentui/react-icons@2.0.335`
- `react` / `react-dom` 16.14.0
- Native `fetch` for the 3rd-party API

Do **not** add: `@fluentui/react` (v8), MUI, Ant, Chakra, `styled-components`, Emotion, Tailwind, axios, lodash, moment, jQuery, Node-only packages, or extra React copies.

Before any new dependency: confirm it runs in the model-driven browser sandbox, has no Node APIs, and will not duplicate React/Fluent (host already injects them). Prefer Fluent v9 components over new packages.

When the real API is added, declare the domain in `<external-service-usage enabled="true">` in `ControlManifest.Input.xml`.
